WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.037 --> 00:00:13.737
heart pounded.

2
00:00:14.378 --> 00:00:17.641
Despite Darb's shouts, Zann was still holding on to the skull.

3
00:00:18.321 --> 00:00:21.804
The energy around him was becoming more violent with every passing second.

4
00:00:22.505 --> 00:00:27.229
If she and the others didn't convince him to drop that skull, its power might destroy him.

5
00:00:28.049 --> 00:00:32.604
Zann glared at a tiny dragon that was harassing Zing.

6
00:00:32.644 --> 00:00:33.845
"Stop!" he intoned, pointing at it.

7
00:00:34.926 --> 00:00:41.130
Blast! The spell singed Zing's tail, and with a yelp, the pet dragon dived behind a pile of

8
00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.031
rubble. "We've got to stop Zann!"

9
00:00:44.412 --> 00:00:44.992
Perda cried.

10
00:00:45.732 --> 00:00:48.354
Without waiting for a response, she leaped at Zann.

11
00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.276
"Oof!" he grunted as she tackled him.

12
00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:57.040
The skull bounced out of Zann's grip and rolled away, coming to rest against the candlestick he had

13
00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:02.677
dropped. Zann's eyes had stopped glowing, and he lay on the floor for a moment, breathing hard.

14
00:01:03.437 --> 00:01:05.580
Then he sat up and looked around the room.

15
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.982
"Zann?" Darb said cautiously.

16
00:01:08.002 --> 00:01:09.203
"Are you okay?"

17
00:01:09.984 --> 00:01:10.965
Zann didn't respond.

18
00:01:11.565 --> 00:01:14.048
Climbing to his feet, he stepped toward the skull.

19
00:01:14.068 --> 00:01:16.470
"No!" Perda shouted.

20
00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:17.772
"Don't touch it!"

21
00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:21.916
"Please, Zann," Gliss said, sobbing.

22
00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:27.267
Grabbing the candlestick, Zann lifted it over his head and brought it down as hard as he could,

23
00:01:27.547 --> 00:01:29.288
smashing the skull to bits.

24
00:01:30.248 --> 00:01:34.791
"No person should ever hold that much power," Zann said in a shaky voice.

25
00:01:35.571 --> 00:01:36.472
He smiled weakly.

26
00:01:36.492 --> 00:01:39.453
"I guess now I know how Morb feels."

27
00:01:40.574 --> 00:01:45.917
Just then a small band of trolls, grunting heavily, rushed through the doorway and into the room.

28
00:01:45.937 --> 00:01:47.457
"Oh no!"

29
00:01:47.858 --> 00:01:48.418
Perda cried.

30
00:01:48.438 --> 00:01:51.680
"It looks like some of the trolls are still under Morb's control!"

31
00:01:52.676 --> 00:01:54.437
"How are we going to get out of here?"

32
00:01:54.877 --> 00:01:55.677
Gliss exclaimed.

33
00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:57.197
Zann smiled.

34
00:01:57.597 --> 00:01:59.098
"Magic—how else?"

35
00:01:59.898 --> 00:02:01.839
He waved toward the remains of the machine.

36
00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:05.059
"Morb can't track us anymore, remember?"

37
00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.600
Gliss quickly zapped herself and Darb away.

38
00:02:09.321 --> 00:02:11.321
Perda grinned and rubbed her fingers together.

39
00:02:11.341 --> 00:02:15.202
"Zap." She landed in a deserted hallway.

40
00:02:15.942 --> 00:02:20.644
Her friends were nowhere in sight, which was not surprising since there hadn't been enough time to agree

41
00:02:20.704 --> 00:02:21.424
on a destination.

42
00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.342
But that didn't matter now that they could use magic.

43
00:02:25.302 --> 00:02:29.885
Perda was about to summon a message moth to track down the others when she heard loud voices

44
00:02:29.926 --> 00:02:36.250
nearby. Curious, she stepped toward the nearest window and discovered that she was on the second floor.

45
00:02:37.131 --> 00:02:39.252
Another machine stood in the courtyard below.

46
00:02:39.272 --> 00:02:43.295
"That must be the magic-sucking machine," thought Perda.

47
00:02:44.015 --> 00:02:47.298
Standing near the machine were two people—Slib and Morb.

48
00:02:47.318 --> 00:02:49.259
"You've failed me!"

49
00:02:49.699 --> 00:02:50.300
Morb shouted.

50
00:02:51.064 --> 00:02:52.825
His face was twisted with anger.

51
00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:57.268
"I'm sorry, Your Majesty," Slib whined.

52
00:02:57.288 --> 00:03:01.752
"I searched all night, but I couldn't catch any leeches.

53
00:03:02.632 --> 00:03:08.016
Every time I displaced the water in the river, they wriggled into the mud before I could catch—"

54
00:03:08.036 --> 00:03:12.039
"First someone tampers with my trolls, and now this!"

55
00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:13.480
Morb interrupted him.

56
00:03:14.368 --> 00:03:20.673
"Schoolchildren all over Magica know how to catch those leeches, and yet you can't manage to bring me

57
00:03:20.713 --> 00:03:22.735
the single one I require?"

58
00:03:24.196 --> 00:03:25.437
Perda frowned, puzzled.

59
00:03:25.857 --> 00:03:28.259
Why did Morb need a single local leech?

60
00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.021
Morb sent a sizzle of energy at Slib.

61
00:03:31.462 --> 00:03:36.185
The energy surrounded Slib for a second, but as far as Perda could tell, it didn't do anything

62
00:03:36.265 --> 00:03:36.586
to him.

63
00:03:37.446 --> 00:03:39.168
Then Morb snapped his fingers.

64
00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:44.642
Perda could hear a loud growl, and a strange striped creature stepped into view.

65
00:03:45.462 --> 00:03:46.203
Slib looked at it.

66
00:03:46.223 --> 00:03:48.644
"Your Majesty," he said.

67
00:03:48.664 --> 00:03:51.345
"What is that?"

68
00:03:51.465 --> 00:03:57.167
"It comes from a world with no magic," Morb said with an evil chuckle.

69
00:03:57.187 --> 00:04:03.810
"Of course, for an experienced Magician such as you, that shouldn't be a problem.

70
00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:09.072
There's just one minor detail "Your Majesty?"

71
00:04:09.672 --> 00:04:10.172
said Slib.

72
00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:11.653
Morb smirked.

73
00:04:11.673 --> 00:04:17.456
"I put a Dousing spell on you—you aren't able to use any magic," he said.

74
00:04:18.296 --> 00:04:20.477
Then he laughed nastily.

75
00:04:20.777 --> 00:04:25.019
Perda ducked out of sight as Slib's screams of terror echoed through the palace.

76
00:04:26.239 --> 00:04:29.041
Meanwhile Zann tiptoed along a windowless corridor.

77
00:04:29.881 --> 00:04:33.843
He knew he should look for his friends, but he couldn't stop thinking about his grandfather.

78
00:04:34.503 --> 00:04:36.444
Boz was somewhere in the palace right now.

79
00:04:37.184 --> 00:04:39.985
He thought about summoning a spy fly to help him locate Boz.

80
00:04:40.685 --> 00:04:41.706
But that would take too long.

81
00:04:42.646 --> 00:04:46.448
Then he remembered a spell that he had learned in Family Spells class a few months earlier.

82
00:04:47.108 --> 00:04:52.290
Closing his eyes, he focused on a memory from when he was five years old—Boz had taken him

83
00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.270
to the ocean for the day.

84
00:04:53.931 --> 00:04:58.192
The two of them were watching a group of giant sea dragons romp in the waves, and Zann

85
00:04:58.212 --> 00:05:00.113
was mesmerized by the enormous creatures.

86
00:05:00.853 --> 00:05:05.615
After a few minutes, he realized his grandfather had been watching him instead of the dragons.

87
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.240
"Why are you looking at me?"

88
00:05:08.721 --> 00:05:09.261
Zann asked.

89
00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.102
Boz smiled warmly.

90
00:05:11.122 --> 00:05:14.683
"You're much more interesting to me than those dragons."

91
00:05:15.483 --> 00:05:20.846
Zann focused on Boz's face from this exact moment, making sure he got every detail right.

92
00:05:20.866 --> 00:05:23.527
"Expand," he murmured.

93
00:05:24.187 --> 00:05:26.808
The image expanded so that Zann could see the background.

94
00:05:27.628 --> 00:05:30.250
Boz was sitting in a stone cell, looking worried.

95
00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:31.730
It was working!

96
00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:35.872
Zann continued to focus, and the image grew larger and larger.

97
00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:41.619
Soon he could see the entire dungeon, and then he could see a stairwell leading to it.

98
00:05:42.359 --> 00:05:49.343
The image continued to expand until it contained the entire palace, including Zann's own current location.

99
00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:56.467
He quickly studied this three-dimensional map and memorized Boz's location five floors below.

100
00:05:56.487 --> 00:05:58.688
"Zap!" Zann said.

101
00:06:00.069 --> 00:06:02.850
He landed in the dark, in the middle of a flight of steps.

102
00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.252
Below he could see light and hear voices.

103
00:06:06.976 --> 00:06:12.641
Hurrying in their direction, Zann found himself in a long corridor lit by torches and lined with many

104
00:06:12.721 --> 00:06:16.964
cells. In every one, red hair glowed in the torchlight.

105
00:06:16.984 --> 00:06:19.807
"Zann?" a familiar voice called out.

106
00:06:20.627 --> 00:06:21.328
Zann smiled.

107
00:06:21.348 --> 00:06:25.171
"Boz!" he shouted, rushing toward his grandfather's cell.
